      "label": "First Mate Maritime Work Attire",
      "clothing_id": "clothing_863b3aa52679",
      "appearance_description": "A single young man in his early twenties standing alone on the weathered deck of a small fishing boat at golden-hour dusk, full body visible from head to toe in a single vertical three-quarter view, one person only, no other people anywhere in frame. Light-medium sun-tanned skin with visible pores, short dark brown messy wind-blown hair, sharp jawline, bright vivid green eyes, lean athletic build. Distinguishing marks clearly visible: small dark mole just below the left ear, faded blue-grey wave-pattern tattoo on the right inner forearm. Wears a storm-grey heavy waxed-canvas maritime work jacket with large round brass snap buttons down the front, sleeves rolled to the elbows; a plain white cotton crew-neck T-shirt underneath; dark canvas cargo work pants with cuffs pushed up; sturdy brown lace-up canvas boots. This is open-sea deck-worker canvas gear, NOT a business suit, NOT a blazer, NOT formal attire. Wind-blown coastal golden-hour light on a weathered wooden fishing boat deck behind him, realistic cinematic live-action film still, photorealistic skin and fabric texture, single subject, no studio backdrop, no multi-view layout, no cartoon, no game look.",
